	(footprint "RocketSenior:MMC5983MA_LGA-16_3x3mm_P0.5mm"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "3d667861-d746-b8a3-cef5-6f22a15c9621")
		(at 162 110.5)
		(descr "MEMSIC MMC5983MA, LGA-16 3x3x1 mm, 0.5 mm pitch, 4 pads per side. Land pattern from MEMSIC MMC5983MA Rev A (4/3/2019) p.20: 0.45 x 0.30 pads, row-to-row 2.550 mm centre-to-centre (+/-1.275). Pad numbering is the CHIP's: pin 1 is the right end of the top row, counter-clockwise from there. Use at 0 deg -- the die then sits datasheet-upright and the mag axes are board axes. Do not substitute Package_LGA:LGA-16_3x3mm_P0.5mm: same copper, but its pad 1 is the top of the left column, which forces a 90 deg part rotation that breaks the pad rectangles (see pcb/README.md).")
